  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Loc Performance founder Victor Vojcek confronted the human cost of shrinking defence orders in 1994. Reduced work had led to layoffs and shorter hours at his factory. He stressed that employees had mortgages, car payments and children at school, while the business sought restoration of funding for tank upgrades.\n\nMeeting military customers' requirements also changed how the company worked. Loc brought painting and packaging in-house to meet specification and shipping requirements. It later converted office space into a product-development centre and expanded into markets including farm equipment, locomotives and hybrid buses, reducing its dependence on defence contracts.",
